# Sync state databases (SQLite plus its write-ahead log / shared-memory sidecars).
# These hold cursors, the dedup index, the Chat store and the failure ledger —
# metadata about your real mailboxes. Never publish one.
state.db
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Credentials. `save` keeps these beside the config (0600), but they can land in
# the working tree while you set things up. All are secrets.
*token*
google-client*.json
google-token*.json
fastmail-token*
# …but never let the credential globs above swallow Go source (e.g. a future
# token.go); secrets have no .go extension.
!*token*.go

# Built binaries. `go build -o save ./cmd/save` drops one at the repo root; a
# bare `go build` inside cmd/save drops one there. NOTE: these are anchored on
# purpose — a bare `save` pattern would also exclude the cmd/save/ source
# directory and silently drop the package from the repo.
/save
cmd/save/save

# macOS noise.
.DS_Store

# Scratch / temp working dirs.
/tmp/
/temp/
/scratch/
*.tmp
